INT. UNDERWATER HABITAT KITCHEN, SEA STATION ALDEBARAN - NIGHT

Steel counters. Portholes full of black. A kettle ticks as it cools.

EZEKIEL "ZEKE" ROMANOV-ABARA (50s, lined face, heavy cardigan) stands at the counter slicing bread into even squares. He sets the knife down. Pipes knock somewhere far off.

He pours a cup of tea. Slides it to the empty place across from him. Waits. It cools. He drinks it himself.

At the porthole, a pale shape glides past: a long, slow, luminous thing. He sees it. He does not remark on it. He folds his hands.

A hatch clunks. TAMSIN VOYLE (30s, shaved head, rubber gloves) comes in, takes a plate from the rack and dries it, though it is already dry. She watches the water rather than him.

He turns the bread over. She turns her back.

ZEKE
Pressure's holding.

TAMSIN
I saw the gauge.

ZEKE
Thought you'd want to know.

TAMSIN
(very evenly)
Fine.

He waits. She adds nothing. She sets the plate down and picks up another. His eyes follow her hand.

He tears a slice of bread in half and holds out one piece. She looks at it for a long time. She takes it. Eats. They both look at the porthole, where the shape has returned and is now circling.

ZEKE (CONT'D)
It follows the light.

TAMSIN
So do we.
